    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0.67,
      type: "MCQ",
      text: `<p></p> <div style="line-height:1.7;"> <p>Assume two end-hosts communicate using the sliding window protocol. The size of the sender window is \\( w \\) bits. Let \\( C \\) be the link bandwidth between the two end-hosts in bps. Further, the round trip time (representing here the time when the first bit of the segment is transmitted till its acknowledgment is received) on the path between the two end-hosts is \\( RTT \\) seconds. </p> <p>If the roundtrip time satisfies \\( RTT &gt; \\frac{w}{C} \\), what is the <b>maximum throughput</b> achieved by the two end-hosts? </p> <p> </p> </div> <p></p>`,
