      text: `<p>A digital computer has a byte-addressable memory unit with \\(16\\) bits per word. The instruction set consists of \\(40\\) different operations. All instructions have an operation code part and two address fields: one for a memory address and one for a register address. This machine has six general-purpose, user-addressable registers. Registers may be loaded directly from memory, and memory may be updated directly from the registers. Direct memory-to-memory data movement operations are not supported. Each instruction is stored in one word of memory. What is the maximum allowable size for memory (assuming all of memory is addressable in an instruction) in words? </p>`,
