    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p>An undirected graph is complete if there is an edge between every pair of vertices. Given a complete undirected graph \\(\\mathrm{G}\\) on \\(n &gt; 2\\) vertices, it can be converted into a directed graph \\(\\mathrm{G}’\\) by choosing a direction for each edge of \\(\\mathrm{G}\\) so that there are no directed cycles \\(\\mathrm{G}’.\\) Which of the following is/are true about \\(\\mathrm{G}’?\\) </p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
