    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p>A tree is a connected acyclic undirected graph.</p> <p>Consider Only the labeled trees on \\(n&gt;2\\) vertices, with distinct labels for vertices from \\(\\{1, 2, \\ldots, n\\}.\\) </p> <p>The Prüfer Code of a Tree is defined as follows:</p> <p>Given a labeled tree \\(\\text{T}\\) with \\(n&gt;2\\) vertices, repeat the following step: </p> <ul> <li>delete the leaf with the smallest label and record the label of its parent until only a single edge remains.</li> </ul> <p>The resulting sequence is called the Prüfer code of the tree.</p> <p>Which of the following is/are true for the Prüfer code of the tree?</p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
