    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p>Consider the following network, which contains a client \\(\\text{A}\\), two routers \\(\\text{B}\\) and \\(\\text{C}\\), and a webserver \\(\\text{D}\\) that listens on port \\(80\\) and does not listen on any other port:<br/> <br/> <img alt="" height="90" src="js/questions/fst-mock-test-2/17.png" width="448"/><br/> <br/> The links \\(\\text{A B, B C}\\) and \\(\\text{C D}\\) have a maximum transmission unit \\(\\text{(MTU)}\\) of \\(9000\\) bytes, \\(1500\\) bytes, and \\(1480\\) bytes respectively.<br/> <br/> For every packet, we are using \\(\\text{TCP}\\) (with no options) and \\(\\textsf{IPv4}\\) (with the \\(\\text{DF}\\) flag set on every packet, and no options). The \\(\\text{TCP}\\) payload contains data that is within the receiver window, and not previously acknowledged. All the checksums are valid, and no data corruption occurs.<br/> <br/> There are \\(4\\) packets sent from \\(\\text{A}\\) to \\(\\text{D}\\) with following parameters - </p> <ul> <li> \\(1\\)st packet: \\(\\text{(TCP)}\\) payload length of \\(1490\\), a \\(\\text{(TTL)}\\) of \\(149.\\) </li> <li> \\(2\\)nd packet: \\(\\text{(TCP)}\\) payload length of \\(222\\), a \\(\\text{(TTL)}\\) of \\(2.\\) </li> <li> \\(3\\)rd packet: \\(\\text{(TCP)}\\) payload length of \\(100,\\) a \\(\\text{(TTL)}\\) of \\(80.\\) </li> <li>4th packet: \\(\\text{(TCP)}\\) payload length of \\(80,\\) a \\(\\text{(TTL)}\\) of \\(3.\\) </li> </ul> <p>Which of the following is/are the CORRECT option?</p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
