        `Suppose \\(\\text{S}\\) and \\(\\text{R}\\) use a stop-and-wait protocol to communicate then the expected number of transmissions of a packet before \\(\\text{S}\\) can send the next packet in sequence \\(=1 / p\\)`,
        `Suppose \\(\\text{S}\\) and \\(\\text{R}\\) use a stop-and-wait protocol to communicate then the expected number of transmissions of a packet before \\(\\text{S}\\) can send the next packet in sequence \\(=\\) \\(1 / \\mathrm{pq}\\)`,
