      type: "MCQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p style="line-height:1.8;">Consider a system with a total of \\(\\mathbf{150}\\) units of memory. Three processes are currently in the system, with their maximum memory needs and current allocations shown below: </p> <p><span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ \\begin{array}{c|c|c} \\textbf{Process} &amp; \\textbf{Max Demand} &amp; \\textbf{Currently Holds} \\\\ \\hline P1 &amp; 70 &amp; 45 \\\\ P2 &amp; 60 &amp; 40 \\\\ P3 &amp; 60 &amp; 15 \\end{array} \$\$ </p> <p style="line-height:1.75;">A new process \\(P4\\) enters the system with a maximum memory requirement of \\(60\\) units.<br/>Depending on its initial request, the state of the system may or may not remain safe. </p> <p style="line-height:1.75;">Which of the following statements correctly describes the safety of the system?</p> <p></p>`,
