      neg: 0,
      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p> <meta/> </p> <div style="line-height:1.9; font-size:16px;"> <p>Two processes compete for entering a critical section using a simple spin lock. Each process follows the pattern <b>entry → critical section → exit</b> exactly <b>once</b>. There is <b>no</b> <code>while(1)</code> or repetition of the critical section; each process tries to enter its critical section only <b>one time</b>. </p> <p>It is possible that the system initially starts with only one of the processes in the ready state, while the other process becomes ready at some later time. (Both processes need not be ready at the start.)</p> <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center; margin:15px 0;"> <div style="border:1px solid #000; padding:12px; width:55%;"> <pre data-pbcklang="c" data-pbcktabsize="4">// ENTRY SECTION\nwhile (test_and_set(t));\n\n// CRITICAL SECTION (executed once)\n\n// EXIT SECTION\nt = 0;\n</pre> </div> </div> <p>The instruction <b>test_and_set(X)</b> is atomic: it returns the old value of <code>X</code> and then sets <code>X = 1</code>. </p> <p style="margin-top:10px;">Consider the following types of schedulers:</p> <ul style="line-height:1.6; margin-left:25px;"> <li><b>Priority scheduler:</b> Higher-priority processes always run before lower-priority ones. </li> <li><b>Round-robin scheduler:</b> Preemptive, each process gets periodic CPU time.</li> </ul> <p style="line-height:1.6;">Which of the following statements is/are correct regarding possible <b>deadlock</b>? (Multiple options may be correct.) </p> </div> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `Under a priority scheduler, deadlock is possible.`,
        `Under a priority scheduler, deadlock cannot occur.`,
        `Under a round-robin scheduler, deadlock cannot occur.`,
        `Under a round-robin scheduler, deadlock is possible.`,
      ],
      answer: ["A", "C"],
      solution: `<img src='js/questions/fst-mock-test-3/27.png' alt='solution' style='max-width:100%; border-radius: 8px;'><br/><img src='js/questions/fst-mock-test-3/27.1.png' alt='solution' style='max-width:100%; border-radius: 8px;'>`
    },
    {
      marks: 1,
      neg: 0,
      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p>A TCP sender is operating with a congestion window of \\(4\\) KB , and the receiver has advertised a window of \\(8\\) KB. At this moment, the sender has transmitted data up to byte number \\(20000\\). The receiver has acknowledged all bytes up to \\(16000\\).<br/>Based on this information, identify which of the following byte numbers are guaranteed to have already been sent by the sender. <b id="docs-internal-guid-35bd31be-7fff-e28f-bb1a-e8575e32575f">Assume 1K</b><b> = \\(10^3\\) </b> </p> <p></p>`,
