      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p> <meta/> </p> <p style="line-height:1.6;">Consider the diagram below which shows only a partial snippet of a weighted undirected graph. There may be additional vertices and edges not shown.</p> <table cellpadding="10" style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;"> <tbody> <tr> <td align="center" style="width: 50%;" valign="top"><img alt="Graph snippet" src="js/questions/fst-mock-test-3/2.png" style="max-width:100%; height:auto;"/></td> <td align="center" style="width: 50%;" valign="middle"> <p style="max-width:90%; text-align:left; line-height:1.6;">Each edge marked with a \\(\\text{?}\\) connects to some unseen vertex. The two edges marked with a \\(\\text{?}\\) are the only edges that connect the shown portion to the rest of the graph. No other information about the remaining graph should be assumed. </p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p style="line-height:1.6;">For the edges shown in the snippet determine whether the following statements are <b>NEVER</b>, <b>ALWAYS</b>, or <b>SOMETIMES</b> true for a minimum spanning tree of the full graph. Here <b>SOMETIMES</b> means that the edge appears in a minimum spanning tree for some valid completions of the unseen part of the graph and does not appear for other valid completions.</p> <p style="line-height:1.6;">Which of the following statements are correct? (Multiple options may be correct.)</p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
