      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p> <meta/> </p> <div style="line-height:1.7;"> <p>If <span> \\(G\\) </span> is a context-free grammar with start symbol <span> \\(S\\) </span>, then <span> \\(G'\\) </span>, the augmented grammar for <span> \\(G\\) </span>, is obtained by introducing a new start symbol <span> \\(S'\\) </span> and the production <span> \\(S' \\rightarrow S\\) </span>.</p> <p>In the context of LR(0) parsers, an LR(0) item (item for short) of grammar <span> \\(G'\\) </span> is a production of <span> \\(G'\\) </span> with a dot at some position of the body.</p> <p>We divide the LR(0) items of <span> \\(G'\\) </span> into two classes:</p> <ol> <li><em>Kernel items:</em> The initial item <span> \\(S' \\rightarrow \\cdot S\\) </span>, and all items whose dots are not at the left end.</li> <li><em>Nonkernel items:</em> All items with their dots at the left end, except for <span> \\(S' \\rightarrow \\cdot S\\) </span>.</li> </ol> <p>Each state of the LR(0) automaton represents a set of items. Which of the following is/are true about the states in LR(0) automaton for grammar <span> \\(G'\\) </span>:</p> </div> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
