    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "NAT",
      text: `<p></p> <p>A B-tree of order \\(M\\) has the following properties: </p> <ul> <li> \\(M\\) denotes the max number of child nodes a node can point to.<br/> </li> <li>The max number of keys per node is \\(M-1\\).<br/> </li> <li>The root node is either a leaf node or an internal node with \\(2\\) to \\(M\\) children and \\(1\\) to \\(M-1\\) keys.<br/> </li> <li>The rest of the internal nodes have between \\(\\left\\lceil \\frac{M}{2} \\right\\rceil\\) and \\(M\\) children.<br/> </li> <li>All leaves are at the same depth, which makes the tree balanced.<br/> </li> </ul> <p>What is the total number of key values stored in the internal nodes of a B-tree of order \\(5\\) with \\(1000\\) leaf nodes? </p> <p></p>`,
