    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "NAT",
      text: `<p></p> <p>Let transactions \\(\\mathrm{T1}\\), \\(\\mathrm{T2}\\), and \\(\\mathrm{T3}\\) be defined to perform the following operations: </p> <ul> <li> \\(\\mathrm{T1}:\\) Add one to \\(A\\)<br/> </li> <li> \\(\\mathrm{T2}:\\) Double \\(A\\)<br/> </li> <li> \\(\\mathrm{T3}:\\) Display the current value of \\(A\\) on the screen and then set \\(A\\) to one </li> </ul> <p>(where \\(A\\) is some numeric item in the database). </p> <p>Suppose the internal structure of \\(\\mathrm{T1}\\), \\(\\mathrm{T2}\\), and \\(\\mathrm{T3}\\) is as indicated below:<br/><span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|} \\hline \\mathrm{T}_1 &amp; \\mathrm{T}_2 &amp; \\mathrm{T}_3 \\\\ \\hline \\begin{array}{c} \\mathrm{F}_1:\\ \\text{fetch } A \\text{ into } \\mathrm{t}_1 \\\\ \\mathrm{t}_1 := \\mathrm{t}_1 + 1 \\end{array} &amp; \\begin{array}{c} \\mathrm{F}_2:\\ \\text{fetch } A \\text{ into } \\mathrm{t}_2 \\\\ \\mathrm{t}_2 := \\mathrm{t}_2 * 2 \\end{array} &amp; \\begin{array}{c} \\mathrm{F}_3:\\ \\text{fetch } A \\text{ into } \\mathrm{t}_3 \\\\ \\text{display } \\mathrm{t}_3 \\end{array} \\\\ \\hline \\mathrm{U}_1:\\ \\text{update } A \\text{ from } \\mathrm{t}_1 &amp; \\mathrm{U}_2:\\ \\text{update } A \\text{ from } \\mathrm{t}_2 &amp; \\mathrm{U}_3:\\ \\text{update } A \\text{ from } 1 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \$\$ <br/>Suppose transactions \\(\\mathrm{T1}\\), \\(\\mathrm{T2}\\), and \\(\\mathrm{T3}\\) are allowed to execute concurrently. If \\(A\\) has initial value zero, how many possible values are displayed by \\(\\mathrm{T3}\\)? </p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
