      text: `<p></p> <p>Let \\(M_{0}, M_{1}, M_{2}, \\ldots\\), be an effective enumeration of all Turing machines. Which of the following problems is (are) decidable? </p> <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman"> <li>Given a natural number \\(n\\), does \\(M_{n}\\) starting with an empty tape halt in fewer than \\(n\\) steps?<br/> </li> <li>Given a natural number \\(n\\), does \\(M_{n}\\) starting with an empty tape halt in exactly \\(n\\) steps?<br/> </li> <li>Given a natural number \\(n\\), does \\(M_{n}\\) starting with an empty tape halt after at least \\(n\\) steps? </li> </ol> <p> </p> <p> </p> <p></p>`,
