    {
      marks: 2,
      neg: 0.67,
      type: "MCQ",
      text: `<p></p> <div style="max-width:900px; margin:20px auto; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height:1.7; color:#111;"> <p>Consider the following definitions of path orders of a binary tree:</p> <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:24px; margin-top:12px; align-items:start;"> <div> <p> \\(\\text{Order A:}\\) </p> <pre class="prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp prettyprinted" data-pbcklang="c_cpp" data-pbcktabsize="4" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="kwd">if</span><span class="pln"> the binary tree </span><span class="kwd">is</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="kwd">not</span><span class="pln"> empty</span><span class="pun">:</span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pun">{</span></li><li class="L2"><span class="pln">  visit the root</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L3"><span class="pln">  traverse the left subtree </span><span class="kwd">in</span><span class="pln"> B</span><span class="pun">-</span><span class="pln">order</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L4"><span class="pln">  traverse the right subtree </span><span class="kwd">in</span></li><li class="L5"><span class="pln">    B</span><span class="pun">-</span><span class="pln">order</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L6"><span class="pun">}</span></li></ol></pre> <p> </p> </div> <div> <p> \\(\\text{Order B:}\\) </p> <pre class="prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp prettyprinted" data-pbcklang="c_cpp" data-pbcktabsize="4" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="kwd">if</span><span class="pln"> the binary tree </span><span class="kwd">is</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="kwd">not</span><span class="pln"> empty</span><span class="pun">:</span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pun">{</span></li><li class="L2"><span class="pln">  visit the root</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L3"><span class="pln">  traverse the right subtree </span><span class="kwd">in</span></li><li class="L4"><span class="pln">    </span><span class="typ">Order</span><span class="pln"> A</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L5"><span class="pln">  traverse the left subtree </span><span class="kwd">in</span></li><li class="L6"><span class="pln">    </span><span class="typ">Order</span><span class="pln"> A</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L7"><span class="pun">}</span></li></ol></pre> <p> </p> </div> </div> <p style="margin-top:30px;">Consider the following binary tree. The path of the binary tree shown is:</p> <p style="text-align:center"><img alt="Binary Tree Diagram" height="227" src="js/questions/fst-mock-test-3/7.png" width="479"/></p> <p style="margin-top:22px;">If the root of the given binary tree is passed to \\(\\text{Order A}\\), what will be the resulting sequence of node visits? </p> </div> <p></p>`,
