      text: `<p></p> <div style="font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; max-width:850px; line-height:1.75;"> <p>A single packet is sent from <b>A</b> to <b>C</b> through <b>B</b>. Propagation delays are: \\(A \\to B = d_1\\) and \\(B \\to C = d_2\\). Assume \\(d_1 \\le d_2\\), and transmission/queueing delays are negligible. </p> <p>Flow control <b>is being implemented in two ways</b>:</p> <div style="display:flex; position:relative; margin-bottom:1.6em;"> <div style="position:absolute; top:2.1em; left:0; right:0; height:1px; background:#000;"> </div> <div style="position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; left:50%; width:1px; background:#000;"> </div> <div style="flex:1; padding-right:1.5rem; padding-top:0.3em;"> <p style="margin:0 0 0.5em 0; font-weight:600; font-size:1.05em;">Case 1: End-to-End Flow Control</p> <div style="font-size:16px; padding-top:1.2em;">Flow control operates only between A and C. The packet travels A → B → C, and C sends back an ACK that travels C → B → A. The entire cycle completes only when A receives the ACK from C.</div> </div> <div style="flex:1; padding-left:1.5rem; padding-top:0.3em;"> <p style="margin:0 0 0.5em 0; font-weight:600; font-size:1.05em;">Case 2: Link-by-Link Flow Control</p> <div style="font-size:16px; padding-top:1.2em;">Flow control operates hop-by-hop. When B receives the packet from A, B immediately sends an ACK to A while simultaneously forwarding the packet to C. When C receives the packet, it sends an ACK to B. The entire cycle completes only when A receives B’s ACK and B has received C’s ACK for the same packet.</div> </div> </div> <hr style="margin:1.2rem 0;"/> <p style="margin-bottom:0.6em; font-size:1.05em;">What is the total time for <b>one complete packet cycle</b> in each case (i.e., time to successfully send one packet from A to C and receive all corresponding ACKs)?</p> <div style="font-size:16px; margin-left:1rem;"> <p><b>A.</b> End-to-End: \\(2(d_1 + d_2)\\), Link-by-Link: \\(d_1 + 2d_2\\) </p> <p><b>B.</b> End-to-End: \\(d_1 + d_2\\), Link-by-Link: \\(d_1 + d_2\\) </p> <p><b>C.</b> End-to-End: \\(2(d_1 + d_2)\\), Link-by-Link: \\(d_1 + d_2\\) </p> <p style="font-size:15px;"><b>D.</b> End-to-End: \\(2d_2\\), Link-by-Link: \\(2d_1 + d_2\\) </p> </div> </div> <p></p>`,
