      text: `<p></p> <p>Consider the following Huffman tree of a message over the \\(5\\)-character alphabet \\(\\text{{A, B, C, D, E}:}\\) </p> <p style="text-align:center"><img alt="" height="271" src="js/questions/fst-mock-test-6/16.png" width="276"/></p> <p>Match the following two columns.</p> <p><span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ \\begin{array}{|ll|ll|}\\hline &amp; \\qquad \\qquad \\textbf{Column 1} &amp;&amp; \\textbf{Column 2} \\\\\\hline \\text{(P)} &amp; \\text{The frequency of A is strictly less} &amp; \\text{(A)} &amp; \\text{True for all messages.} \\\\ &amp; \\text{ than the frequency of B.} \\\\ \\text{(Q)} &amp; \\text{The frequency of C is greater} &amp; \\text{(B)} &amp; \\text{False for all messages.} \\\\ &amp; \\text{than or equal to the frequency of A.} \\\\ \\text{(R)} &amp; \\text{The frequency of D is strictly} &amp; \\text{(C)} &amp; \\text{Depends on the message.} \\\\ &amp; \\text{greater than the frequency of A.} \\\\ \\text{(S)} &amp; \\text{The frequency of D is greater than or} &amp; \\\\ &amp; \\text{equal to that of A, B, and C combined.} \\\\\\hline\\end{array} \$\$ </p> <p></p>`,
