      text: `<p></p> <p>Consider two nodes, \\(\\text{A}\\) and \\(\\text{B}\\). Suppose the network path from \\(\\text{A}\\) to \\(\\text{B}\\) has a bandwidth of \\(5 \\mathrm{~KB} / \\mathrm{s} \\;(5,000\\) bytes per second ) and a propagation time of \\(120 \\mathrm{~msec}\\). The path in the reverse direction, from \\(\\mathrm{B}\\) to \\(\\mathrm{A}\\), has a bandwidth of \\(10 \\mathrm{~KB} / \\mathrm{s}\\) and a propagation time of \\(80 \\mathrm{~msec}\\). Let data packets have a size (including all headers) of \\(500\\) bytes and acknowledgment packets a size of \\(100\\) bytes. </p> <p>What will be the throughput (in Bytes/sec) A can achieve in transmitting to \\(\\text{B}\\) using Stop-and-Wait? You can treat a \\(500\\)-byte data packet as transferring \\(500\\) bytes of useful data. </p> <p></p>`,
