      text: `<p></p> <p>Suppose a router \\(\\mathrm{R} 1\\) receives an IP packet of \\(552\\) bytes, and has to fragment the packet and forward the fragments across a network with an MTU of \\(300\\) bytes. Then, a subsequent router \\(\\text{R}2\\) has to further forward the packet (and/or any resulting fragments) onto another network that has an MTU of \\(100\\) bytes. Here, the MTU refers to the size of the largest packet that can be carried in a link-layer frame. Let the size of the TCP header is \\(20\\) bytes and that of the IP header is also \\(20\\) bytes. </p> <p>Which of the following is/are CORRECT options regarding the fragments sent by \\(R1\\) and \\(R2\\) ? </p> <p></p>`,
