      text: `<p></p> <p>Consider the following grammar for generating binary fractions.<br/> <span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ \\begin{aligned} &amp; \\text{F} \\rightarrow 0 . \\text{B} \\qquad\\{\\text{F.val = B.val}\\} \\\\ &amp; \\text{B}_0 \\rightarrow 0 \\text{B}_1 \\qquad\\{\\text{X}\\} \\\\ &amp; \\text{B}_0 \\rightarrow 1 \\text{B}_1 \\qquad\\{\\text{Y}\\} \\\\ &amp; \\text{B} \\rightarrow 0 \\qquad \\{\\text {B.val }=0\\} \\\\ &amp; \\text{B} \\rightarrow 1 \\qquad \\{\\text{B.val}=1 / 2\\} \\\\ \\end{aligned} \$\$<br/> What should be the missing semantic actions \\(\\text{X}\\) and \\(\\text{Y}\\) to calculate the decimal value of an input string? </p> <p>Recall that the numeric value of a binary fraction \\(0. \\text{b}_1 b_2 \\ldots b_n\\) is calculated as \\(\\sum_{i=1}^n b_i 2^{-i}\\). Each non-terminal has a synthesized attribute \\(\\text{val}\\) that is used to store its value. The final value should be returned in \\(\\text{F.val.}\\) </p> <p></p>`,
      image: "",
