9"><span class="pln">       </span><span class="kwd">return</span><span class="pln"> mystryrecur</span><span class="pun">(</span><span class="pln">tmp</span><span class="pun">,</span><span class="pln"> x</span><span class="pun">);;</span></li><li class="L0"><span class="pln">   </span><span class="pun">}</span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pln">   </span><span class="kwd">else</span></li><li class="L2"><span class="pln">   </span><span class="pun">{</span></li><li class="L3"><span class="pln">       head </span><span class="pun">→</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="kwd">next</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="pun">=</span><span class="pln"> mystryrecur</span><span class="pun">(</span><span class="pln">head </span><span class="pun">→</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="kwd">next</span><span class="pun">,</span><span class="pln"> x</span><span class="pun">);</span></li><li class="L4"><span class="pln">       </span><span class="kwd">return</span><span class="pln"> head</span><span class="pun">;</span></li><li class="L5"><span class="pln">   </span><span class="pun">}</span></li><li class="L6"><span class="pun">}</span></li></ol></pre> <p>Let the linked list be following and head points to the first node of the linked list.<br/> <span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ 0 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 6 \\rightarrow \\text { NULL } \$\$<br/> What will be the result of the linked list after executing the following line and accessing it through the \\(\\textsf{“head"}\\) pointer? </p> <pre class="prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp prettyprinted" data-pbcklang="c_cpp" data-pbcktabsize="4" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="pln"> head </span><span class="pun">=</span><span class="pln"> mystryrecur</span><span class="pun">(</span><span class="pln"> head</span><span class="pun">,</span><span class="pln"> </span><span class="lit">2</span><span class="pun">);</span><span class="pln"> </span></li></ol></pre> <p></p>`,
