      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p> <meta/> </p> <p>Two processes execute concurrently and attempt to implement mutual exclusion using two different locking mechanisms, namely <b>LockA</b> and <b>LockB</b>.</p> <p>For <b>LockA</b>, a shared variable \\( \\texttt{turn} \\) is used to decide whose turn it is. The variable is initially set to \\( \\texttt{turn} = 0 \\). </p> <p>For <b>LockB</b>, interrupts are disabled during the critical section. The system consists of a single processor unless stated otherwise.</p> <p>The functions \\( \\texttt{disableInterrupts()} \\) and \\( \\texttt{enableInterrupts()} \\) respectively disable and enable interrupts on the given processor. </p> <p>The code fragments executed by the processes are shown below. For simplicity, the code for Process \\(P_0\\) and Process \\(P_1\\) is written separately for <b>LockA</b>. </p> <div style="font-size:90%;"><span class="mjx-chtml MJXc-display" style="text-align: center;"></span> \$\$ \\begin{array}{c|c|c} \\text{LockA – Process } P_0 &amp; \\text{LockA – Process } P_1 &amp; \\text{LockB – Process } P_0 \\text{ and } P_1 \\\\ \\hline \\\\[-4pt] \\begin{aligned}[t] &amp;\\text{/* turn initially = 0 */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{while (turn == 1);} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{/* Critical Section */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{turn = 1;} \\end{aligned} &amp; \\begin{aligned}[t] &amp;\\text{/* turn initially = 0 */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{while (turn == 0);} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{/* Critical Section */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{turn = 0;} \\end{aligned} &amp; \\begin{aligned}[t] &amp;\\text{/* Code for both } P_0 \\text{ and } P_1 \\text{ */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{disableInterrupts();} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{/* Critical Section */} \\\\ &amp;\\texttt{enableInterrupts();} \\end{aligned} \\end{array} \$\$ </div> <p>Which of the following statements about the above locking mechanisms is/are <b>TRUE</b>?</p> <p></p>`,
